# UI spacing

Apply this guide when creating or updating ScreenTake settings UI:

- Use 12 points between a label and its associated control, horizontally or vertically.
- Use 20 points between separate features or settings groups.
- Use `Spacing.labelToControl` and `Spacing.featureGap` from the design tokens.
- Set spacing explicitly; do not rely on native picker label spacing.
- Keep icon-to-label and spacing inside a single control separate from these rules.
- Settings sidebar buttons use 40 × 40 point targets, with 20 points between items.

SwiftUI uses logical points for these design dimensions (12px / 20px in the design guide).
